-- The TARGETED userspace waiver for NORM-LOG-SPEC ruling N9: each waiver and cure names the book it answers,
-- and the guard reads every default with RECALL ALL. Written by the N9 skeptic, 2026-10-09; tutorial in
-- specs/todo/norm-log-waiver-userspace-draft.md. Not goldened; run with `l4 run`.
-- E3 (one of two defaults waived) must block; E3b (both waived) must allow.
IMPORT prelude

DECLARE Person IS ONE OF patron, librarian
DECLARE Action IS ONE OF
  `return` HAS bk IS A NUMBER
  payFine HAS bk IS A NUMBER
              tm IS A NUMBER
  borrow HAS bk IS A NUMBER
             tm IS A NUMBER
  waive HAS bk IS A NUMBER
            tm IS A NUMBER

DECLARE Mark HAS mbk IS A NUMBER
                 mtm IS A NUMBER

GIVEN b IS A NUMBER
      d IS A NUMBER
GIVETH DEONTIC Person Action
loanOf MEANS
  PARTY patron MUST `return` b WITHIN d
  HENCE FULFILLED
  LEST  RECORD `overdue` IS Mark b d
        HENCE PARTY patron MUST payFine b t WITHIN 100
              HENCE RECORD `cured` IS Mark b t
              HENCE FULFILLED

GIVETH DEONTIC Person Action
waiverPower MEANS
  PARTY librarian MAY waive b t WITHIN 200
  HENCE COMMIT `waived` IS Mark b t
  HENCE waiverPower

GIVEN now IS A NUMBER
      marks IS A LIST OF Mark
      b IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`marked by` MEANS any (GIVEN m IS A Mark YIELD m's mbk EQUALS b AND m's mtm AT MOST now) marks

GIVEN now IS A NUMBER
      m IS A Mark
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`this default continuing at` MEANS
      m's mtm AT MOST now
  AND NOT `marked by` now (RECALL ALL patron's `cured`) (m's mbk)
  AND NOT `marked by` now (RECALL ALL OFFICIAL's `waived`) (m's mbk)

GIVEN now IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`some default continuing at` MEANS
  any (GIVEN m IS A Mark YIELD `this default continuing at` now m) (RECALL ALL patron's `overdue`)

GIVETH DEONTIC Person Action
borrowing MEANS
  PARTY patron MAY borrow 2 t PROVIDED NOT `some default continuing at` t WITHIN 200

GIVETH DEONTIC Person Action
two MEANS loanOf 1 14 RAND loanOf 3 50 RAND waiverPower RAND borrowing

-- E3: default A (book 1) waived at 25; default B (book 3) late at 60, never waived; borrow at 70. Should be blocked.
#TRACE two AT 0 WITH
  PARTY patron DOES `return` 1 AT 20
  PARTY librarian DOES waive 1 25 AT 25
  PARTY patron DOES `return` 3 AT 60
  PARTY patron DOES borrow 2 70 AT 70
-- E3b: both waived: allowed
#TRACE two AT 0 WITH
  PARTY patron DOES `return` 1 AT 20
  PARTY librarian DOES waive 1 25 AT 25
  PARTY patron DOES `return` 3 AT 60
  PARTY librarian DOES waive 3 65 AT 65
  PARTY patron DOES borrow 2 70 AT 70
